  status_reading: weakened
  evidence_id: EV-CERTBIN-db7f15
  decision_id: DEC-20261003-34a65b
  proposed_by: idea-generator
  title: >-
    After quotienting a k-orbit E_0 base by tau^2 + tau + 2, the
    informative collision count at n=19 matches the birthday count
    (delta = 0) to within a factor 2

  statement: >-
    CLAIM (heuristic validation at a toy cell; NO ATTACK; NO EXPONENT
    MOVE). Setting: Koblitz curve E_0: y^2 + xy = x^3 + 1 over F_{2^19}
    with modulus t^19+t^5+t^2+t+1, #E = 523492 = 4*130873, r = 130873
    prime (re-measured in Stage 0; a mismatch is O-ARTIFACT). The
    Frobenius endomorphism satisfies tau^2 + tau + 2 = 0, so for every
    subgroup point P the geometric relation [2]P + tau^2(P) + tau(P) = O
    is the zero log-row in F_r. HEUR-1: after deleting that kernel, the
    sum map on unordered 3-multisets of a target-independent k-orbit
    physical-point base (k in {2,3}) is indistinguishable from a uniform
    random function into the prime-order subgroup as judged by colliding
    pairs. Precisely: C_eff is the smallest integer whose birthday
    expectation C_eff(C_eff-1)/(2r) lies in [5, 50]; C_eff distinct
    3-multisets are drawn uniformly from the k-orbit union; the number
    of informative colliding pairs (difference vector not in the
    characteristic-kernel span over F_r) divided by that expectation
    lies in [1/2, 2] on every frozen n=19 seed. A ratio >= r^{0.05} on
    every n=19 seed is the exponent reading and falsifies delta = 0 at
    this cell only. Predicted time exponent remains 1/2. The
    conditional (1-delta)/2 is a falsification branch, not a claimed
    speedup. n=17 is a nearby object with split cyclotomic block and
    is not pooled with n=19. No Certicom instance is solved.

  mechanism: >-
    OBJECT FRAME. Representation R1: k normal-basis (equivalently
    Frobenius-orbit) masks of a target-independent factor base.
    Membership is the <tau, -1> orbit union of k prime-order points.
    Operation set Sigma: addition of base-orbit points together with
    Frobenius acting as lambda on logs. Trichotomy: partial-action.
    LOSSY PROJECTION: discard the particular weight-3 vector and keep
    its class modulo tau^2 + tau + 2. The discard is Sigma-compatible
    because every generator of the kernel is the zero log-row. OPEN
    NUMBER: the ratio of informative colliding pairs to C(C-1)/(2r)
    at C_eff with expectation in [5, 50]. OFF-LIMITS: F2 is the
    relation vector used as a component; F6 is the Frobenius action
    used as a component. What is added is the quotient collision
    exponent delta, predicted 0.

  assumptions:
    - The curve is E_0 with trace -1, so the polynomial is tau^2 + tau + 2.
      A random binary curve is a different kernel and is not a substitute.
    - k-orbit means the union of the <tau, -1> orbits of k subgroup points.
      Orbit size is logged; using B = k*n instead of the physical-point
      count is an artifact.
    - n=19 is the measurement cell. n=17 is the nearby object and is not
      a replicate. Composite odd order at n=17, if observed, is recorded
      and does not falsify HEUR-1 at n=19.
    - Amazon Bedrock is prohibited. No AUXIN provisioning.
    - Full-cost S stays null. A collision among base points is not a
      solved public target.

  proof_search_map:
    bottleneck: >-
      Supply of informative F_r-rows among a k-orbit base. If that
      supply is only the birthday supply, no relation phase exists
      below Theta(sqrt(r)) samples.
    baseline_embedding:
      parameter_slice: >-
        Archived m=83 expectations C(C-1)/(2 r_83) = 7.832e-12 and
        8.868e-11 at (B, m) = (332, 3) and (498, 3) are not re-measured.
        The toy slice is n=19, m=3, k in {2,3}, C_eff with birthday
        expectation in [5, 50].
      reproduction_check: >-
        Verify [2]P + tau^2(P) + tau(P) = O on two subgroup points
        before counting rows. A failure means the kernel lemma was
        applied to the wrong curve.
    observation_collision:
      observable: >-
        Informative rank / colliding-pair count after deleting the
        kernel spanned by the characteristic relation of each orbit.
      distinct_preimage_search: >-
        A kernel vector and a non-kernel collision are two preimages
        of "a linear dependence". They are counted separately.
    constructive_transforms:
      - transform: stronger_invariant
        proposed_object: >-
          The relation module modulo (tau^2 + tau + 2), rather than
          the raw multiset count.
        predicted_gain: >-
          Removes trivial rows. Predicted collision count stays the
          birthday count (delta = 0).
    quantifier_order: >-
      FOR ALL prime degrees of E_0: the characteristic relation is
      the zero log-row. Separately, at the n=19 cell, FOR ALL frozen
      seeds the informative/birthday ratio lies in [1/2, 2]. The
      conditional exponent claim has the opposite quantifier and is
      not asserted.
    method_ceiling:
      strongest_certifiable_claim: >-
        Either the informative collision count matches the birthday
        count at n=19 to within a factor 2, or it does not. A match
        does not prove the same match at m=83. A mismatch of factor
        r^{0.05} at one degree does not by itself prove an exponent
        at m=131.
      nearby_object_control: >-
        n=17 (ord_17(2)=8, cyclotomic block splits) is the nearby
        object and is not pooled. A relabelled Z/rZ sample is the
        second control: delta must read as 0 there or the instrument
        is broken.
    proof_obligations:
      - claim: tau^2 + tau + 2 = 0 on E_0 and the log-row is zero in F_r
        responsibility: correctness
      - claim: birthday expectation C(C-1)/(2r) under a uniform random sum map
        responsibility: success_probability
      - claim: sample count to first collision is Theta(sqrt(r)) when delta = 0
        responsibility: runtime
      - claim: the kernel transfers to every prime degree; delta does not
        responsibility: scope
    not_applicable_reason: null
  rerandomization: null
  asymptotic_claim: null
  heuristic_assumptions:
    - id: HEUR-1
      formal_statement: >-
        After quotienting by tau^2 + tau + 2, the sum map on the
        remaining unordered m-multisets of a k-orbit base on E_0 at
        n=19, m=3, k in {2,3}, with C_eff chosen so the birthday
        expectation lies in [5, 50], is indistinguishable from a
        uniform random function into the prime-order subgroup as
        judged by colliding pairs: the informative count is within
        a factor 2 of C_eff(C_eff-1)/(2r) on every frozen seed.
      random_model_justification: >-
        The classical birthday theorem gives the expectation exactly
        for a uniform random function. The kernel lemma is an
        endomorphism identity. The random-function half is the
        imitation that delta = 0 asserts.
      supporting_results:
        - >-
          Endomorphism identity tau^2 + tau + 2 = 0 on E_0 (internal:
          IDEA-20260930-d2d20c; n=19 order 4*130873 in
          EXP-BINSTD-5d3ec0/stage0/n19-order-check.yaml).
        - >-
          Birthday / occupancy for a uniform random function (classical;
          recalled, not opened).
      validation_experiment_ids:
        - EXP-CERTBIN-9ea3d0
      falsification_condition: >-
        Every n=19 seed and k in {2,3} has informative/birthday ratio
        >= r^{0.05}, with the Z/rZ control still inside [1/2, 2].
  structural_ingredients:
    - description: >-
        E_0 Frobenius satisfies tau^2 + tau + 2 = 0, so the corresponding
        log-row is the zero functional in F_r.
      citation: ledger/proposals/IDEA-20260930-d2d20c.yaml
