      citation: experiments/EXP-BINSTD-5d3ec0/stage0/n19-order-check.yaml
      provenance: internal
      verified_by: coordinator session 2026-10-03, file read
      role: toy cell order
    - description: >-
        Expected colliding pairs of a uniform random function of size C
        into a group of order r equal C(C-1)/(2r).
      citation: birthday theorem / balls and bins (classical; no source opened)
      provenance: recalled
      verified_by: null
      role: birthday prediction
  reduction_chain:
    core_problem: >-
      Informative collision count of a k-orbit base after the
      characteristic kernel is deleted, at n=19 only.
    corollaries: []
  predictions:
    - metric: informative_collisions_over_birthday
      direction: lower
      minimum_effect: >-
        ratio in [1/2, 2] on every n=19 seed and k in {2,3}; a ratio
        >= r^{0.05} on every such cell is the exponent reading
    - metric: kernel_rows_that_are_nonzero_in_F_r
      direction: lower
      minimum_effect: zero such rows; any nonzero kernel row voids the quotient
    - metric: zr_control_ratio
      direction: lower
      minimum_effect: in [1/2, 2]; outside that band the instrument is not read
  test_boundary:
    instances:
      - n=19 E_0, k in {2,3}, seeds 2026100301 and 2026100302
      - Z/rZ control seed 2026100303
      - n=17 nearby object, reported apart
    parameters:
      n_measure: 19
      n_nearby: 17
      m: 3
      k: [2, 3]
      curve: E_0
      A: 0
      B: 1
      birthday_band: [5, 50]
    implementation: experiments/EXP-CERTBIN-9ea3d0/implementation/run.py
    budget:
      maximum_runs: 3
      maximum_memory_gb: 4
      maximum_workers: 1
  falsification_conditions:
    - The kernel check fails on E_0 at n=19.
    - The Z/rZ control reports a ratio outside [1/2, 2].
    - Every n=19 seed and k has ratio >= r^{0.05} (delta=0 false at n=19).
  interpretation_limits:
    - >-
      Predicted exponent remains 1/2. The conditional (1-delta)/2 is a
      falsification branch, not a claimed speedup.
    - >-
      Transfer to m=83 or m=131 is the kernel identity only. delta
      requires a new measurement. Archived cells have expected
      collisions about 1e-11.
    - >-
      KN-OPEN-020 class is implicit-membership via orbit rotation. Not a
      claim that every implicit base works.
    - Full-cost S stays null. No n=53 wall-clock ratio is cited.
    - >-
      Does not reopen EXP-BINSTD-8bdf86 ell89 or EXP-BINSTD-591d28 H1
      factor-4 reject_scoped bands.
  dominated_by: >-
    Frobenius-class Pollard rho (KR-RHO-037e22) dominates this object on
    time, memory, and queries at every outcome this cell can certify.
  sota_delta:
    time: >-
      Predicted 0 versus rho (delta = 0). Unclaimed branch would be a
      factor r^{delta/2} on the relation-phase sample count only, not
      on a solved target.
    memory: Enumerated image at the toy C_eff only; r^{0} attack memory.
    data_queries: No challenge queries.
  status_note: >-
    Analyzed under DEC-20261003-34a65b / EV-CERTBIN-db7f15 after Stages
